BT 1 0 0 1 0 87.2 Tm /F1 8.8 Tf 12 TL (Redis shipped seven security releases on 23 Jul after researchers - using Kimi K3 AI agents - found multiple zero-days and) Tj T* (built working authenticated RCE exploits. The chains \(CVE-2026-25243, CVE-2026-23479, CVE-2026-25588,) Tj T* (CVE-2026-25589, CVE-2026-23631\) all abuse the RESTORE command: a crafted serialised payload triggers invalid memory) Tj T* -0.076371 Tw (access, and a Redis Streams shared-ownership bug lets a corrupt RDB object be double-freed, which the published script turns) Tj T* 0 Tw (into arbitrary memory access and ultimately invokes system\(\). Working PoCs exist for stock Redis 6.2.22, 7.4.9, 8.6.4 and) Tj T* (8.8.0; no in-the-wild exploitation reported. Apply the seven updates, keep Redis off the internet with auth + network) Tj T* (segmentation, and revoke RESTORE from accounts that do not strictly need it \(this cuts off both disclosed paths\). Notable as) Tj T* (an example of LLM-agent vulnerability discovery producing real exploits.) Tj T* ET
